1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
So my first idea was to organize these settings in a simple two-dimensional layout using rectangles.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The horizontal direction shows different Execution Modules.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Inside each module, a Pattern connects Agents in a certain structure.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The vertical direction shows Execution Behaviors, which apply across the system.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The key difference is simple: an Execution Module, or Pattern, moves the system forward.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
An Execution Behavior does not move the system forward on its own.
